{
  "conversation_lines": [
    {
      "turn_number": 1,
      "time": "2198-11-28 03:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Hi, I’m Dr. Lee. You’re in the ICU because your blood sugar was very high and you’re in diabetic ketoacidosis. We’ve started you on fluids and insulin through an IV to help correct that."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 2,
      "time": "2198-11-28 03:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay… I’ve been here before for this. I took my Lantus this morning and used my sliding scale, but I just couldn’t keep anything down."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 3,
      "time": "2198-11-28 03:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, your glucose was 637 when you arrived, and your anion gap was elevated, which confirms DKA. We’re giving you an insulin drip now to bring that down safely."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 4,
      "time": "2198-11-28 03:06:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ve been nauseous all day. Started vomiting around 7 p.m. I didn’t eat much. Is that why this happened?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 5,
      "time": "2198-11-28 03:08:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s likely a big part of it. Poor intake and vomiting can throw off your insulin balance. We’re also treating your nausea with Zofran and Compazine."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 6,
      "time": "2198-11-28 03:10:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’m still feeling shaky and my heart’s racing. Is that from the DKA?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 7,
      "time": "2198-11-28 03:12:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, the high blood sugar and dehydration can cause tachycardia—your heart rate is 129. We’re watching it closely. It should improve as we correct your fluids and sugars."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 8,
      "time": "2198-11-28 03:15:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We also saw some peaked T-waves on your EKG, and your potassium was high at 5.6. We’re monitoring that carefully to prevent any heart rhythm issues."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 9,
      "time": "2198-11-28 03:17:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Oh, that’s scary. Is it dangerous?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 10,
      "time": "2198-11-28 03:19:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We caught it early. Your levels are coming down with treatment. No signs of a heart attack—we checked your enzymes and they were normal."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 11,
      "time": "2198-11-28 03:21:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Good. I’ve had so many DKA episodes because of my gastroparesis. The Botox didn’t help much last time."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 12,
      "time": "2198-11-28 03:23:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "I see you had an EGD with Botox recently. Unfortunately, it sounds like it hasn’t provided lasting relief. We’re focusing on symptom control for now."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 13,
      "time": "2198-11-28 03:25:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I noticed some dark flecks in my vomit. Is that blood?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 14,
      "time": "2198-11-28 03:27:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Possibly. Given your history of esophagitis, it could be from irritation in your esophagus. We’ve started you on an IV proton pump inhibitor to protect your stomach lining."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 15,
      "time": "2198-11-28 03:29:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Should I be worried about bleeding?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 16,
      "time": "2198-11-28 03:31:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your hemoglobin is stable. The dark flecks are likely old blood. We’ll keep an eye on it, but you’re not showing signs of active bleeding."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 17,
      "time": "2198-11-28 06:10:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning. Your labs from a few hours ago show your glucose is down to 217 and your anion gap is closing. That’s a great sign."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 18,
      "time": "2198-11-28 06:12:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s good. I feel a little less shaky. Can I eat something?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 19,
      "time": "2198-11-28 06:14:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Not yet. We want to make sure your nausea is under control and your sugars stay stable. We’ll try small sips later if you’re doing well."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 20,
      "time": "2198-11-28 06:16:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay. I’ve been off my blood pressure meds—metoprolol and lisinopril. Should I restart them?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 21,
      "time": "2198-11-28 06:18:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We held them initially because your blood pressure and heart rate were high from DKA. Once you’re more stable, we’ll restart them."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 22,
      "time": "2198-11-28 10:15:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We got your urine test back. There was a possible E. coli, so we started you on cipro just in case."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 23,
      "time": "2198-11-28 10:17:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I don’t have any burning when I pee. Could it be a false alarm?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 24,
      "time": "2198-11-28 10:19:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Possibly. The lab noted contamination from skin flora, so it might not be a real infection. We’ll repeat the test and stop antibiotics if it’s negative."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 25,
      "time": "2198-11-28 14:30:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "The repeat urine culture showed contamination again. No true UTI. We’re stopping the cipro."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 26,
      "time": "2198-11-28 14:32:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Great, I didn’t want to take more antibiotics. I’m still on metronidazole—should I stop that too?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 27,
      "time": "2198-11-28 14:34:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You were supposed to finish that course a few days ago. Since you’re still taking it, we’ll have you stop now to avoid unnecessary side effects."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 28,
      "time": "2198-11-29 07:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your anion gap is now normal, and your blood sugars are between 150 and 200. We’re switching you from the insulin drip to subcutaneous insulin."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 29,
      "time": "2198-11-29 07:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "So I’ll go back to my Lantus and Humalog?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 30,
      "time": "2198-11-29 07:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes. You’ll get 30 units of Lantus at bedtime and use Humalog as a sliding scale four times a day. We’ll monitor your levels closely."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 31,
      "time": "2198-11-29 07:06:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s what I was on before. I hope it keeps me stable."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 32,
      "time": "2198-11-29 11:45:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We did a chest X-ray today. No signs of pneumonia. Your lungs look clear, which is good news."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 33,
      "time": "2198-11-29 11:47:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I had pneumonia last time I was here. I was worried it came back."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 34,
      "time": "2198-11-29 11:49:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "No, your lungs are clear. The previous opacity has resolved. This time, your DKA was triggered by gastroparesis, not infection."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 35,
      "time": "2198-11-29 15:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You tolerated a small meal earlier without vomiting. That’s a big improvement."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 36,
      "time": "2198-11-29 15:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, I actually felt hungry. Can I eat more?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 37,
      "time": "2198-11-29 15:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll advance your diet slowly—soft foods first. Your nausea has improved, so that’s promising."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 38,
      "time": "2198-11-29 15:06:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’m glad. I hate being on IV fluids. When can I go home?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 39,
      "time": "2198-11-29 15:08:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "If you keep doing well—eating, stable sugars, no vomiting—we’re looking at discharge tomorrow or the day after."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 40,
      "time": "2198-11-30 08:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your labs this morning are excellent. Anion gap closed, no ketones, sugars 100–180. You’ve had two meals without issues."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 41,
      "time": "2198-11-30 08:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s great. What about my blood pressure meds?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 42,
      "time": "2198-11-30 08:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ve restarted your metoprolol and lisinopril. Your blood pressure is now well-controlled."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 43,
      "time": "2198-11-30 08:06:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And the Nexium? I wasn’t taking it, but I know I should."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 44,
      "time": "2198-11-30 08:08:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re switching you to pantoprazole 40 mg daily. It’s similar and will help with your esophagitis and those dark flecks in your vomit."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 45,
      "time": "2198-11-30 12:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re doing so well. We’re planning to discharge you tomorrow morning."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 46,
      "time": "2198-11-30 12:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s a relief. What should I watch for at home?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 47,
      "time": "2198-11-30 12:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Monitor your blood sugar closely. If you start vomiting again or can’t keep food down, check for ketones and come in early."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 48,
      "time": "2198-11-30 12:06:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I will. Should I follow up with my endocrinologist?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 49,
      "time": "2198-11-30 12:08:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, within a week. Also with GI to discuss long-term options for your gastroparesis. The Botox hasn’t helped much, so other treatments may be needed."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 50,
      "time": "2198-12-01 09:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning. All set for discharge. You’re on Lantus 30 units at bedtime, Humalog sliding scale, and your other meds as we discussed."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 51,
      "time": "2198-12-01 09:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Got it. No changes, right?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 52,
      "time": "2198-12-01 09:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Exactly. Continue everything as prescribed. Take the pantoprazole daily, even if you feel fine."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 53,
      "time": "2198-12-01 09:06:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I will. Thank you for helping me get through this again."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 54,
      "time": "2198-12-01 09:08:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re welcome. Stay hydrated, eat small meals, and don’t hesitate to call or come in if things go off track."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 55,
      "time": "2198-12-01 09:10:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ll be careful. I don’t want to be back here soon."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 56,
      "time": "2198-12-01 09:12:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll do our best to prevent that. Take care, and I’ll see you in follow-up."
    }
  ],
  "summary": {
    "admission_start": "2198-11-28 02:45:00",
    "admission_end": "2198-12-01 11:40:00",
    "summary_paragraph": "A woman with a history of Type 1 diabetes, gastroparesis, and esophagitis was admitted for diabetic ketoacidosis triggered by poor oral intake and vomiting. She was treated in the ICU with an insulin drip, which was transitioned to subcutaneous insulin as her anion gap closed and blood sugars stabilized. Nausea and vomiting improved with antiemetics, and she advanced to a soft diet. A possible UTI was ruled out due to urine contamination, and antibiotics were discontinued. Her home antihypertensives were restarted, and she was switched to pantoprazole for esophagitis. She was discharged home in stable condition with instructions to continue her insulin regimen, take pantoprazole daily, and follow up with endocrinology and gastroenterology.",
    "problems": [
      "Diabetes with ketoacidosis, type I [juvenile type], uncontrolled",
      "Diabetes with neurological manifestations, type I [juvenile type], uncontrolled",
      "Gastroparesis",
      "Esophageal reflux",
      "Esophagitis, unspecified",
      "Unspecified essential hypertension",
      "Tachycardia, unspecified"
    ]
  }
}
